WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.839
You already use AI. You ask a question, you get an answer, and you copy it somewhere.

2
00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:10.638
That's useful. It's also the smallest version of what these tools can do.

3
00:00:11.138 --> 00:00:12.404
Take one ordinary task.

4
00:00:12.404 --> 00:00:19.117
Every Monday, someone pulls last week's campaign numbers into a spreadsheet, writes a summary, and sends it to the client.

5
00:00:19.117 --> 00:00:21.758
It takes an hour. It happens fifty times a year.

6
00:00:22.258 --> 00:00:25.977
Doing the work means you get a little faster at that hour.

7
00:00:25.977 --> 00:00:28.735
You ask a chatbot to help with the summary.

8
00:00:28.735 --> 00:00:30.081
You save ten minutes.

9
00:00:30.081 --> 00:00:32.197
Next Monday, you do it all again.

10
00:00:32.697 --> 00:00:37.246
Directing the work looks different. You describe the outcome once.

11
00:00:37.246 --> 00:00:38.555
One agent plans it.

12
00:00:38.555 --> 00:00:43.654
Another builds a small tool that pulls the numbers and drafts the summary.

13
00:00:43.654 --> 00:00:45.446
A third checks the result.

14
00:00:45.946 --> 00:00:48.473
Now the report writes itself every Monday.

15
00:00:48.473 --> 00:00:53.586
Your job is to read it, decide whether it's right, and approve it before it goes out.

16
00:00:54.086 --> 00:00:57.786
The skill changes. It stops being "I can do this task."

17
00:00:57.786 --> 00:01:02.092
It becomes "I can get this built, and I know whether it's good."

18
00:01:02.592 --> 00:01:04.833
That's what this guide teaches. Let's start.
